# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <LinkList>
    <three slot="three" />
    <other-component slot="name" />
  </LinkList>
  <one>
    <two slot="two" />
  </one>
</template>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-ignore.vue:4:12 lint/nursery/noVueDeprecatedSlotAttribute ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The slot attribute is deprecated.
  
    2 │ <template>
    3 │   <LinkList>
  > 4 │     <three slot="three" />
      │            ^^^^^^^^^^^^
    5 │     <other-component slot="name" />
    6 │   </LinkList>
  
  i Vue 3 treats it as a regular attribute, so the content goes to the component's default slot instead of the named slot.
  
  i Use the v-slot directive on a <template> element instead, for example <template v-slot:name> or <template #name>.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

